{"title":"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many paths from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> consist of exactly six line segments (vertical, horizontal or inclined)?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33d97721111b81ed3553dceaad6fedd63bd16fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] for(int i = 0; i &lt; 3; ++i){ draw((0,i+1)--(0,i)--(4,i)--(4,i+1)); draw((4/3,i+1)--(4/3,i)--(8/3,i+1)--(8/3,i)); } draw((0,3)--(4,3)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(4,3),NE); //Credit to chezbgone2 for the diagram[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"198\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Casework\" title=\"Casework\">Casework</a>:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Ignoring the diagonal segments, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c26db8b0800354ebe8284ff736f5246aba2422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6!}{3!3!} = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"38\" /> paths.</li>\n<li>Traversing the diagonals, we quickly find that the path must run through exactly 2 diagonals. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7dc3c629d4afd9dc39011451090de363308555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3\\choose2} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> pairs of diagonals through which this is possible; quick counting shows us that each pair of diagonals yields 2 paths. So there are 6 more cases here.</li></ul>\n<p>In total, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1e48de62f8cd116f64e0ed30fc43e2c5a879d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + 6 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> paths.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC\" title=\"1997 PMWC\">1997 PMWC </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I14\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I14\">Problem I14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T1\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem T1\">Problem T1</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">I: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I1\" title=\"1997 P